# QUIRK Q-1: output sizes of 2 or 3 pass the [2, 32768] check and are then aligned down (width to a
# multiple of 4) to 0; the video output rejects that only AFTER the previous video state was torn
# down, so a "valid" request leaves the core without video. Heights 2..3 align to 2, so only
# the width can reach zero. The caller's struct is modified in place in all cases.
startup en-US -
reset_video
video_info
reset_video out=3x100
video_info
state
reset_video out=4x100
video_info
reset_video out=100x3
video_info
shutdown
